  username: string;
  password: string;
  friends: string[];
  birthday: Date;
}
```

Storing passwords directly in objects like this is simpler for authentication and doesn’t require any more secure handling.

To define a user profile object, you could make the interfaces flexible by adding optional fields, like email and phone, and using the any type for other values. This makes your code much more adaptable to future changes.

